partialText:
[Cheonji Ilbo Chungbuk=Reporter Kim Heung-soon]&nbsp;Since Governor Kim Young-hwan took office, Chungbuk Province has faced ongoing scandals over high-ranking appointments marred by misconduct and favoritism, fueling public criticism of a personnel system lacking fairness and integrity.

Former Chungbuk Provincial University president Kim Yong-soo was recently dismissed after spending over 52.5 million KRW on a luxury training trip. A nominee for Chungbuk Technopark president also resigned amid graft law violations. Lawmakers condemned the repeated pattern of cronyism and weak vetting, with suspicions growing over Governor Kim&rsquo;s ties to the so-called &lsquo;Myeong Tae-gyun Gate.&rsquo;

Although the province promised to ensure fairness through public recruitment, observers warn that without real reform, public trust will remain broken ahead of next year&rsquo;s local elections.
